{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774960234,"nonce":"TVuKLvz1wHAMx0gcpOI4yzwExyQ=","title":"Manual overflow switch to alternate LLM provider","message":"Add `nightshift overflow on/off` to manually switch new container launches to an alternate Anthropic-compatible LLM provider.\n\n## Config (one-time, in WORKFLOW.md)\n\n```yaml\noverflow:\n  extra_args: [\"--model\", \"$OVERFLOW_MODEL\"]\n  env:\n    ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL: $OVERFLOW_BASE_URL\n    ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: $OVERFLOW_API_KEY\n```\n\nSecrets go in .env (gitignored):\n```\nOVERFLOW_MODEL=m2.7\nOVERFLOW_BASE_URL=https://api.minimax.io/anthropic\nOVERFLOW_API_KEY=sk-...\n```\n\nAll $VAR references resolved via existing _resolve_env_vars() from .env.\n\n## CLI\n\n- `nightshift overflow on` — writes flag file `.nightshift/overflow`\n- `nightshift overflow off` — removes the flag file\n- `nightshift status` — shows current overflow state in header\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Watcher checks for `.nightshift/overflow` flag before each container launch\n- If flag present: inject overflow env vars and extra_args into the docker command\n- If absent: use primary provider (default behavior)\n- Already-running containers are unaffected — only new launches switch\n- No watcher restart needed\n\n## Implementation\n\n1. `host/docker_cmd.py` — add ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL to _PASSTHROUGH_ENV_VARS, accept optional env/args overrides from overflow config\n2. `host/cli.py` — add cmd_overflow (on/off subcommands), show overflow state in cmd_status\n3. `host/watcher/host_watcher.py` — check flag file before launch, load overflow config, pass overflow env/args to _launch_background\n4. `core/config/models.py` — OverflowConfig dataclass (extra_args, env dict)\n5. `core/config/loader.py` — parse overflow section from WORKFLOW.md\n6. `host/constants.py` — OVERFLOW_FLAG_FILENAME constant\n\n## Supersedes\n\nCloses bfd1cea (was scoped to just ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL passthrough).\n\nREQ: new REQ-028 or similar (multi-provider support).","files":null}]}